{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Methods · Bay Area Landfill Methane Watch{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h2>Methods</h2>
<p>
  A hierarchical Bayesian model turns sparse, detection-limited overpasses into an estimate of
  how often each site emits above a floor and how much while it does. Every overpass counts,
  including those where nothing was seen, weighted by each instrument's chance of seeing a plume
  of a given size. Sites share information, so sites with few overpasses get wide intervals
  rather than forced numbers.
</p>
<p>
  Repairs are checked by comparing a site's emissions before and after a documented repair date,
  against control sites seen by the same instruments. A drop is reported only when the posterior
  probability of a decrease is at least 0.975; otherwise the result is inconclusive, shown with
  its interval.
</p>

<h3>Validation</h3>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for v in validations %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ v.path }}</code><br>{{ v.title }}</td><td>{{ v.result }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Run manifest</h3>
<pre>{{ manifest }}</pre>
{% endblock %}
